Track 2: "Did You Calibrate the Tripod for the Teargas?"
- Story & Context: Hidden in an abandoned billboard tower over the expressway, Elena confessed to the crew that she had stolen the signal box keys from her transit-cop brother, her hands trembling so severely that she dropped her glass slide onto the asphalt three stories down. To steady her nerves, the band spent an hour silently tracking the transit of Jupiter's red spot using an optical finder scope taped to a microphone stand. When the police sirens breached the perimeter, she slammed her bare thumb against the rusted fretboard, screaming the confession over an undulating planetary synth chord: "I stole the keys to burn the route, so look up before we bleed."
