Track 3: Sankofa Over Apogee
- Story & Context: Weeks after the protest was broken up, legends spread that the gantry amplifiers on the northern overpass had never actually shut off, continuing to siphon stray current into an unending loop of talking drums and fuzz feedback. A lone night-watchman named Isaac claimed he mounted the highest billboard with his daughter’s toy telescope and watched the transit lights synchronize themselves to the orbit of the evening star. As dawn burned away the diesel mist, the rusted speakers sighed out one last soaring choral refrain through the highlife guitars: "What was stolen by the road will return upon the orbit."
